# The build-context ignore file for the nais image.
#
# It is a copy of public muninn's `.dockerignore` MINUS the `bots/` line, and it
# exists because those two requirements cannot live in one file. The public repo
# must exclude `bots/`: the folders are gitignored, one of them carries NAV
# configuration, and a developer building locally must not bake whichever bots
# happen to be on their laptop into an image. This deployment must INCLUDE
# exactly one bot folder, or `discoverAllBots()` finds nothing and the process
# exits 1 — a CrashLoopBackOff, not an empty chat.
#
# BuildKit resolves `<dockerfile-name>.dockerignore` in preference to
# `.dockerignore`, so the deploy workflow copies this file next to the checked-out
# public `Dockerfile` as `Dockerfile.dockerignore` and the public repo is never
# edited. Measured on Docker 29.6.2, both directions:
#
#     .dockerignore excludes bots/          → [build] NO BOTS
#     + Dockerfile.dockerignore (this file) → [build] bots present: <name>
#                                             docker run … ls /app/bots → <name>
#
# Keep it in sync with the public `.dockerignore` when that file changes. The
# only intended difference is the missing `bots/` line.
node_modules/
.git/
.env
*.test.ts
coverage/
models/
.DS_Store
